module Mizan

# Design tokens, the module registry and the string catalogue. All singletons:
# there is exactly one palette, one list of modules and one language per process.
singleton Tokens 1.0 Tokens.qml
singleton Destinations 1.0 Destinations.qml
singleton Strings 1.0 Strings.qml

# The action trace, as QML writes to it: one guarded facade over `app.diag` so
# that a component can log without knowing whether a bridge is attached.
singleton Diag 1.0 Diag.qml

# Shell.
NavRail 1.0 NavRail.qml
NavRailItem 1.0 NavRailItem.qml
ChromeButton 1.0 ChromeButton.qml
PageHost 1.0 PageHost.qml
DialogHost 1.0 DialogHost.qml
AppDialog 1.0 AppDialog.qml

# One action in the window's title bar, contributed by the page on screen:
# glyph, word and the function key that also fires it. See the file's header
# for why the shortcuts live in the title bar row at all.
TitleAction 1.0 TitleAction.qml

# What the till's wall is wearing — column count and card shape — published by
# PosPage and read by the arrange screen, which must show the same wall.
singleton TileMetrics 1.0 TileMetrics.qml

# The question asked before something irreversible: the figures it will change, the
# conditions it cannot undo cleanly, and a button that says the verb. One component,
# because every destructive act in the app was asking with its own hand-rolled
# Yes/No and none of them said what was at stake.
ConfirmDialog 1.0 ConfirmDialog.qml

ToastHost 1.0 ToastHost.qml

# Page furniture, shared by every list page.
IconButton 1.0 IconButton.qml
GlyphButton 1.0 GlyphButton.qml
PageHeader 1.0 PageHeader.qml
FilterBar 1.0 FilterBar.qml
DateField 1.0 DateField.qml

# Every field that holds a price, a cost or a quantity. One type, because the one
# thing all twenty of them were missing was the same thing: selecting the existing
# value when the field takes focus, so the first keystroke replaces it. See the
# file's own header for why that is not a nicety on a till.
NumberField 1.0 NumberField.qml

# The section selector inside a record: sales / payments on a customer, invoices /
# payments on a supplier, the three halves of the product editor. Named SectionBar
# rather than SelectorBar because FluentControls registers that name too, and a
# file importing both modules could not then say which one it meant.
SectionBar 1.0 SectionBar.qml

# Find one product: a field whose matches drop under it, plus a button that lists
# the whole catalogue. The till had this interaction and the stocktake and the stock
# ledger needed the same one — so it lives here rather than three times.
ProductFinder 1.0 ProductFinder.qml

# The select-product table: every fact a picker row carries, under a heading per
# column, filtered as the operator types. One body, three shells — the till's
# product_select dialog, this popup for every screen that asks from inside a
# dialog, and nothing else, so "which product" is answered the same way at the
# till, over a delivery, over a stocktake, over a ledger and inside the
# multi-unit form.
ProductPicker 1.0 ProductPicker.qml
ProductPickerPopup 1.0 ProductPickerPopup.qml

# The select-product surface: one table — name, barcode, category, stock, price —
# behind every place a product is chosen from. ProductPicker is the table itself,
# for a caller that owns the frame; ProductPickerPopup is that table in a popup,
# for a caller that only has a screen. See each file's header for the split.
ProductPicker 1.0 ProductPicker.qml
ProductPickerPopup 1.0 ProductPickerPopup.qml

# One delivery line entered whole — quantity, cost, selling price — with the keypad
# typing straight into whichever figure has focus. A popup rather than a workflow
# dialog, because it opens from inside one.
LineEntry 1.0 LineEntry.qml

# Take an amount against something owed, with the keypad and the "left after this"
# figure that a partial payment has to say out loud. One component, four callers: a
# till sale, a delivery, a customer account, a supplier account.
PaymentEntry 1.0 PaymentEntry.qml

# A titled, tinted panel around a group of fields. A caption is a NAME for a group; a
# panel is a group — an edge, a background and an icon instead of ten grey pixels.
FormGroup 1.0 FormGroup.qml

# KPI strip. CardRow is the wrapping layout, KpiCard is what goes in it.
CardRow 1.0 CardRow.qml
KpiCard 1.0 KpiCard.qml

# Charts. ChartCard is the frame; the three plots are the only three shapes the
# reports and dashboard screens ask for. Named DonutChart / LineChart / BarsH
# rather than PieChart / AreaChart / BarChart because QtCharts and QtGraphs
# register those names, and a file importing both modules could not then say
# which one it meant — the same collision SectionBar was renamed for above.
# charts.js gets no entry, for the reason columns.js does not.
ChartCard 1.0 ChartCard.qml
DonutChart 1.0 DonutChart.qml
LineChart 1.0 LineChart.qml
BarsH 1.0 BarsH.qml

# Data. columns.js gets no entry here: a .pragma library is imported by relative
# path from the file that uses it, not resolved through the module.
DataTable 1.0 DataTable.qml
RowActions 1.0 RowActions.qml
PaginationBar 1.0 PaginationBar.qml

# The two "nothing to show" layers.
StateView 1.0 StateView.qml
LoadingOverlay 1.0 LoadingOverlay.qml

# POS. The till screen is decomposed rather than written as one page: pos.py is
# ~1450 lines, well past the 800-line ceiling, and most of what is inside it is
# reusable furniture rather than till logic.
#
# CommandRail is gone: its five heroes were the tall command column the till's
# redesign removed, and nothing else used it. The actions it held live in the
# transaction panel's compact toolbar now.
Numpad 1.0 Numpad.qml
KeypadDisplay 1.0 KeypadDisplay.qml
CategoryStrip 1.0 CategoryStrip.qml
PosTile 1.0 PosTile.qml
CartLine 1.0 CartLine.qml
TotalsDock 1.0 TotalsDock.qml
PayButton 1.0 PayButton.qml

# Shared with the purchase screen, which selects a supplier the same way.
# PartyCard is the surface — who is attached, the ✕ and the chevron. PartySelect
# wraps it with the searchable list that drops under it, which is how both the till
# and a delivery attach one: the dialog it replaced covered the cart and the note it
# was being attached to.
PartyCard 1.0 PartyCard.qml
PartySelect 1.0 PartySelect.qml

depends QtQuick
depends QtQuick.Controls
depends QtQuick.Layouts
depends QtQuick.Shapes
depends QtQuick.Templates
depends QtQuick.Window
depends FluentControls
